# AI-Powered CAD Generation for Mechanical Engineering

## Overview
This project presents a startup concept for an AI-powered platform that automatically converts photographs, sketches, or scanned drawings into editable 3D CAD models and engineering documentation.
The solution is designed to simplify the reverse engineering process, reduce manual modeling time, and improve productivity in mechanical engineering and manufacturing environments.
The concept combines Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, CAD automation, and Industry 4.0 principles into a single engineering platform.

## Project Goals
The proposed solution aims to:
- automate creation of 3D CAD models from images;
- reduce engineering design time;
- simplify reverse engineering workflows;
- improve accessibility of CAD technologies for SMEs;
- support digital transformation in manufacturing.

## Key Features
- Image-to-CAD conversion using AI
- Automatic feature recognition
- Parametric 3D model generation
- Engineering drawing generation
- Cloud-based processing
- Integration with Industry 4.0 workflows

## Target Users
- Mechanical engineers
- Manufacturing companies
- Design bureaus
- CAD designers
- Industrial enterprises
- Engineering freelancers
- Educational institutions

## Market Analysis
The startup concept includes a preliminary business analysis based on:
- Total Addressable Market (TAM)
- Serviceable Available Market (SAM)
- Serviceable Obtainable Market (SOM)
- Customer segmentation
- Early adopter identification
Estimated market evaluation demonstrated significant growth potential for AI-assisted engineering design solutions.

## Business Model
The proposed monetization strategy combines:
- SaaS subscription
- Enterprise licensing
- API integration
- Custom industrial solutions

## Technology Stack (Concept)
- Artificial Intelligence
- Computer Vision
- Deep Learning
- CAD Systems
- Cloud Computing
- REST API
- Python
- PyTorch / TensorFlow (planned)
- AWS / Google Cloud (planned)

## Expected Benefits
The proposed platform is expected to:
- reduce manual CAD modeling effort;
- accelerate product development;
- improve engineering productivity;
- lower reverse engineering costs;
- increase accessibility of digital manufacturing technologies.

## Project Status
Startup Concept / Academic Business Project
The project represents a validated startup concept developed as part of an innovation and entrepreneurship course. 
It includes technical, market, and financial feasibility analysis but is not an implemented software product.
